-- NORM-LOG N10 goal A, lockstep operands: acceptance test (GM's dinner race, 2026-10-26).
-- Pass: the same table as dinner-roll-alice-bob.l4. Before A this roll gave X1 [2] (a read seeing a
-- purchase stamped after it), X2 [2,2] and X4 Bob [1,1].
IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    opened
    taken
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `reads the ledger`
    `buys dinner`

diners MEANS LIST Bob, Alice
closing MEANS 75600

-- What an act does, then back to that diner's own chain.
GIVEN d IS A Party
      act IS AN Act
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`after` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `reads the ledger` THEN
        RECORD d's `entries read` IS count (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
        RECORD d's `taken seen`   IS elem taken (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
        `evening of` d
    WHEN `buys dinner` THEN
        COMMIT `dinner status record` IS taken
        `evening of` d

-- One chain per diner, recursing into itself only.
GIVEN d IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`evening of` MEANS
    PARTY d
    MAY    act
    WITHIN 0 OF closing
    HENCE  `after` d act

-- The same rule for both diners; each diner's FIRST act enters that diner's chain.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the evening` MEANS
    EVERY d IN diners
        MAY    act
        WITHIN 0 OF closing
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  `after` d act

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the arrangement` MEANS
    COMMIT `dinner status record` IS opened
    HENCE `the evening`

-- Main trace: Alice reads 65100, Bob buys 65160, Alice reads 65220.
-- X0 (control, no purchase by anyone): Alice reads at 65100 and 65220
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES `reads the ledger` AT 65100
    PARTY Alice DOES `reads the ledger` AT 65220

-- X1 (future purchase): Alice reads at 65100; Bob buys LATER, at 70000
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES `reads the ledger` AT 65100
    PARTY Bob   DOES `buys dinner`      AT 70000

-- X2 (the requested timeline): read 65100, Bob buys 65160, read 65220
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES `reads the ledger` AT 65100
    PARTY Bob   DOES `buys dinner`      AT 65160
    PARTY Alice DOES `reads the ledger` AT 65220

-- X3 (same-branch control): Alice reads 65100, Alice buys 65160, Alice reads 65220
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES `reads the ledger` AT 65100
    PARTY Alice DOES `buys dinner`      AT 65160
    PARTY Alice DOES `reads the ledger` AT 65220

-- X4 (mirror): Bob reads 65100, Alice buys 65160, Bob reads 65220
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY Bob   DOES `reads the ledger` AT 65100
    PARTY Alice DOES `buys dinner`      AT 65160
    PARTY Bob   DOES `reads the ledger` AT 65220
